title: The confession goal seeks the player out — only outside conversation
story: character-acceptance
author: Sharpee Platform
seed: 42
description: ADR-318 Acceptance 3, seek-out leg composed with ADR-310 D16.
  The confession goal activates at breaking but a conversation in
  progress suppresses pursuit: while the player keeps asking, the
  Steward does not move or confess. After the player leaves and the
  conversation window (4 turns) lapses, he seeks the player out and the
  confession fires where the player is.
  Run: node dist/cli/sharpee.js --test
    --story stories/character-acceptance/chord/b3-conscience.story
    stories/character-acceptance/tests/transcripts/b3-seek-out.transcript

---

# Five maintained lies climb to breaking (15..75); the goal is active
# from the crossing — but every ask keeps the conversation fresh, so
# pursuit stays suppressed: no confession, no movement
> ask steward about the ledger
[OK: contains "balance to the penny"]

> ask steward about the ledger
[OK: contains "balance to the penny"]

> ask steward about the ledger
[OK: contains "balance to the penny"]

> ask steward about the ledger
[OK: contains "balance to the penny"]

> ask steward about the ledger
[OK: contains "balance to the penny"]
[OK: not contains "cannot carry it"]

# Still in conversation at breaking: another ask, still suppressed
> ask steward about the ledger
[OK: contains "balance to the penny"]
[OK: not contains "cannot carry it"]

# The player walks away; the conversation window starts lapsing
> north
[OK: contains "Hall"]

# Inside the window the Steward holds — quiet turns, no confession
> wait
[OK: not contains "cannot carry it"]

> wait
[OK: not contains "cannot carry it"]

> wait
[OK: not contains "cannot carry it"]

> wait
[OK: not contains "cannot carry it"]

# The window lapses: he has sought the player out — the confession
# fires in the HALL, where the player is, not where the lies were told
> wait
[OK: contains "cannot carry it any longer"]

> look
[OK: contains "Steward"]
